[TITLE] Self-monitoring of an isolated power station
[P1] On a difficult-to-reach plateau, a station feeds a dispensary a radio relay, weather instruments and safety lighting The micro-network brings together solar panels, lithium batteries and a small diesel generator As the road may remain closed for several days, a controller measures the voltage, current. temperature and vibration every 200 milliseconds. Detailed data remains in place: only a compressed summary is transmitted when the link is operational Medical and communication equipment is a priority
[P2] On October 18, 2025, a dust storm reduced solar output by 34 percent in fifteen minutes. The temperature of the battery compartment has risen by 8°C. While the inverter fan was producing an abnormal vibration instead of shutting down the station. The system turned off the secondary heating, reduced some of the lights and started the rescue group. He identified three possible causes of the debris on the panels, a worn bearing and increasing resistance in a battery connector. After the storm, a head-worn camera read the license plates and alarm codes, then a local processor compared them to the offline manual.
============================================================

